{"title":"1989 APMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_APMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be a set consisting of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> of positive integers with the property that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/b/27b1492ff113138ec4ce535cf238cdb1ea61bc1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq a &lt; b \\leq n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"112\" height=\"17\" />. Show that there are at least\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/5/03583c73c9bb05c7d8b20bd053e14e8fa07dd3e9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4m \\cdot \\dfrac{(m - \\dfrac{n^2}{4})}{3n}\\]\" width=\"114\" height=\"59\" />\ntriples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d9e22097e20a1249b5332202b24941a4bf9e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a53387373f79f3f15a70abeeb58639c7d60aa2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10fe40b98e74737c70752abaa29332bc3369bfd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" /> belong to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_APMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017181616\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.006 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.007 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 55/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1775/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:21659:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017181616 and revision id 158163. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}